Moves are observable: MapUnit.moveObserver (an IMoveObserver, MapUnit.cs) is told of every step a unit takes in MapUnit.Move (a move, the last step of a won attack, or a retreat), after the unit is on its new tile and before it enters it (OnEnterTile). The engine sends no animation messages while animations are off, so without this a headless UI cannot show the other civs' units walking: they jump from where they were to where they end the turn. The observer is called synchronously and changes nothing: no state, no draw from GameData.rng, so games replay as before.

--- a/C7Engine/C7GameData/MapUnit.cs
+++ b/C7Engine/C7GameData/MapUnit.cs
